Futuristic hybrid Chinese architecture with Chinese-style negative space (Liubai)::Oriental landscape architecture that is walkable, habitable, and scenic::Jiejing (borrowed scenery), Kuangjing (framed scenery), Zhangjing (obstructed scenery), Liubai (void)::Architectural phenomenology and spirit of place::Tadao Ando's silent geometry::Louis Kahn's monumentality::Carlo Scarpa's detail and boundary awareness::Aldo Rossi's archetype and memory::Critical regionalism::Minimalist volumes and large empty spaces::Figure-ground relationship::Sublime aesthetics::Shrouding and revealing::Grand architectural scale::Always one area of clear light::Deep shadows, mist, aerial perspective::Low-saturation composite colors::At least one highly recognizable color element as a visual anchor::Restraint, silence, sacred, unexplained surreal space::Cinematic award-winning lens composition::Ultra-wide angle lens

Theme: {argument name="theme" default="Chang'e flying to the moon"}

Ratio 16:9

Build a brand quote poster around a central quote. Organize the screen into a dark rounded information panel with a high-energy colored border. Place bold, blocky opening quotation marks in the top section and giant, subtle closing quotation marks in the bottom section. The quote should be in a light, geometric sans-serif font, left-aligned in 3-4 lines. Use a high-brightness accent color for the border and opening quotes, with a very deep low-brightness color for the main panel background. The style should be clean digital vector with no gradients or shadows. 
---
